# Comment hygiene

When editing source here, comments and docstrings must describe the **code**,
not the review/release process. This rule exists only to surface the policy at
edit time; the policy itself — with a worked example — lives in one place:
[`development/style.md` → "Comments"](../../development/style.md#comments).
{% if glob == '**/*' %}
> `paths` is `**/*` because `primary_language` (`{{ primary_language }}`) has no
> language-specific glob mapped. Narrow it to your real source extensions (e.g.
> `**/*.{ext}`) so this rule only fires on code, not on docs or config.
{%- endif %}
